cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "JKinco Listen (Open Edition)"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Wenxuan
    family-names: Zhang
    alias: wenxuanzhang1209-cyber
repository-code: "https://github.com/wenxuanzhang1209-cyber/jkinco-listen-open"
url: "https://wenxuanzhang1209-cyber.github.io/jkinco-listen-open/"
abstract: >-
  A local-first AI workbench that turns meeting recordings into finished, formatted minutes.
  Speech recognition, scene detection, minutes generation, and quality review all run on the
  user's own machine, with no API key and no outbound model calls. Includes evidence-gated
  meeting-type detection so that a document template asserting legal responsibility cannot be
  applied on generic evidence alone.
keywords:
  - meeting-minutes
  - speech-to-text
  - local-first
  - privacy
  - self-hosted
  - asr
  - llm
